# Packages strapd installs from the AUR, kept apart from strapd-base.packages
# because they are built on the target rather than pulled from a repo. yay is in
# here and is also what installs the rest, so it has to be bootstrapped from its
# PKGBUILD first; nothing else in this file can be resolved before it exists.
#
# Hardware-conditional AUR packages are listed here too so the ISO builder sees
# them, even though install/hardware/* only reaches for them on matching machines.
#
# Nothing here can be installed by strapd-pkg-add: it runs `pacman -S`, and
# install/* calls it as root inside the target, where yay refuses to run at all.
# So this file is a list of what needs building, not something install/* can act
# on. Where that build happens, a repo, a chroot step in the ISO build, or a
# first-boot pass as the user, is still undecided.

aether
asusctl
cliamp
herdr
lib32-nvidia-580xx-utils
limine-mkinitcpio-hook
limine-snapper-sync
localsend
macbook12-spi-driver-dkms
mangowc
mise-bin
nvidia-580xx-dkms
nvidia-580xx-utils
qmk-hid
tensaku
ttf-ia-writer
tuxedo-drivers-nocompatcheck-dkms
tzupdate
ufw-docker
xdg-terminal-exec
yaru-icon-theme
yay
yt6801-dkms
